<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/77/0043> <https://schema.org/pagination> "43"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/77/0043> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 13 Ch 77: Conditions of entitlement, membership of the household and normal amount payable — PDF page 43\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68401a731d85c6606009cce4/dmgch77.pdf#page=43).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nRounding of fractions\n77376 Where the calculation of Amount A or Amount B results in a fraction of a penny, it should be\n\nrounded in the claimant’s favour1. So when calculating\n\n\n1. Amount A (as in DMG 77371), any fraction should be rounded up to the next whole penny, if in the\nclaimant’s favour and\n\n\n2. Amount B (as in DMG 77373), any fraction should be rounded down to the next whole penny, if in the\nclaimant’s favour.\n\n\n                                                                                    1 SPC Regs, reg 7(4);\n\n\n77379 - 77999\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
