<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/77/0059> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 13 Ch 77: Conditions of entitlement, membership of the household and normal amount payable — PDF page 59\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68401a731d85c6606009cce4/dmgch77.pdf#page=59).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nPrescribed percentages\n45 Prescribed percentages from 6.04.20\n\n\nFor the purposes of determining\n\n\n1. The MSC (see DMG 77363) 60%\n\n\n2. Amount A (see DMG 77371 2.) 60%\n\n\n3. Amount B (see DMG 77373 1.) 40%\n\n\nMaximum savings credit from 6.04.20\n46 The MSC is a fixed percentage of the difference between the SMG and the SCT (see DMG 77363).\nFrom 6.04.20, that percentage is 60%.\n\n\nSo from 6.04.20 the amount of the MSC is as follows\n\n\n1. claimant with no partner £173.75 SMG - £150.47 SCT x 60% = £13.97\n\n\n2. claimant with a partner £265.20 SMG - £239.17 SCT x 60% = £15.62\n\n\n3. polygamous marriages £265.20 SMG - £239.17 SCT x 60% = £15.62\n\n\n4. prisoners Nil\n\n\n5. members of religious orders fully maintained by their order (see DMG 78680) Nil\n\n\n6. people in hospital - see DMG 78700.\n\n\n\n\nGuarantee credit from 12.04.21\n\nStandard minimum guarantee (see DMG 77331)\n47 Amount of SMG from 12.04.21\n\n\n1. Claimant who has no partner £177.10\n\n\n2. Claimant and one partner (if appropriate) £270.30\n\n\n3. Each additional spouse in a polygamous marriage case £93.20\n\n\n4. Prisoners Nil\n\n\n5. Members of religious orders fully maintained by their order Nil\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
