<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0072> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 13 Ch 78: State Pension Credit: additional amounts and special groups  — PDF page 72\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e10327f5069cdc54868955/dmg-Ch-78.pdf#page=72).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nPersons residing with the claimant 78500 - 78529\n\n\n\nIntroduction 78500\n\n\nDefinition of a non-dependant 78501 - 78509\n\n\nPeople who are not non-dependants 78510 - 78514\n\n\nAmount of deduction 78515\n\n\nNon-dependants who have partners 78516 - 78518\n\n\nNon-dependant of more than one joint occupier 78519 - 78520\n\n\nNon-dependant deduction not appropriate 78521 - 78523\n\n\nCalculation of a non-dependant's gross income 78524 - 78529\n\n\n\n\nIntroduction\n\n78500 Where non-dependants live with the claimant, a deduction from the allowable housing costs may\n\nbe appropriate1. A deduction should be considered for each non-dependant or group of non-dependants,\n\nbut only one deduction can be applied to each non-dependant 2.\n\n\n                                                 1 SPC Regs, Sch II, para 14; 2 SPC Regs Sch II, para 14(2A)\n\n\n\nDefinition of a non-dependant\n\n78501 With the exception of those people mentioned in DMG 78510, non-dependants are people aged\n\n18 or over who normally reside with the claimant1.\n\n\n                                                                          1 SPC Regs, Sch II, para 1(4) & 14\n\n\nMeaning of normally resides\n78502 A person normally resides where they usually live. Periods of residence or absence that are of an\nexceptional nature should be disregarded. A person who is temporarily absent from their normal home,\ncontinues to normally reside where they usually live and with the people they usually live with.\n\n\n78503 When considering where a person normally resides the DM should have regard to\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
