<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0078> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 13 Ch 78: State Pension Credit: additional amounts and special groups  — PDF page 78\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e10327f5069cdc54868955/dmg-Ch-78.pdf#page=78).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\ndependant deduction.\n\n\n                                1 SPC Regs, Sch II, para 14(6)(a); 2 Sch II, para 14(6)(b); 3 Sch II para 14(7)(dd);\n                                                 4 Sch II, para 14(7)(a); 5 Sch II, para 14(7)(b); E & T Act 73, s 2;\n                        Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990, s 2;6 SPC Regs, Sch II, para 14(7)(c);\n                                            7 Sch II, para 14(7)(d); 8 Sch II, para 14(7)(g); 9 Sch II, para 14(7)(e);\n                                                                  10 Sch II, para 14(7)(cc); 11 Sch II, para 14(7)(f);\n\n\nDeduction appropriate – UC non-dependants\n78522 Where a non-dependant is entitled to UC and is\n\n\n1. aged 25 or over or\n\n\n2. aged less than 25 and has earned income\n\n\na deduction at the rate described in Appendix 1 will be appropriate.\n\n\n78523\n\n\n\nCalculation of a non-dependant’s gross weekly income\n\n78524 [see DMG memo 02/25][See Memo DMG 04-25] [See Memo DMG 06/25] [See Memo DMG 08-\n25] When calculating the gross weekly income of a non-dependant (see DMG 78515 and Appendix 1 to\n\nthis Chapter), disregard1 any\n\n\n1. “AA”\n\n\n2. DLA\n\n\n3. PIP\n\n\n4. ADP\n\n\n5. AFIP\n\n\n6. payments made under, or derived from\n\n\n         6.1 the Macfarlane Trust\n\n\n         6.2 the Macfarlane (Special Payments) Trust\n\n\n         6.3 the Macfarlane (Special Payments) (No. 2) Trust\n\n\n         6.4 the Fund\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0079> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "6.5 the Eileen Trust 6.6 the Independent Living Fund (2006) (but see note) 6.7 the Skipton fund 6.8 the Caxton Foundation 6.9 MFET Limited 6.10 any income from capital received from the London Emergencies Trust (LET) and the We Love Manches" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
