<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0114> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 13 Ch 78: State Pension Credit: additional amounts and special groups  — PDF page 114\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e10327f5069cdc54868955/dmg-Ch-78.pdf#page=114).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nsupersession at the same time as any SPC. The DM deciding SPC should make sure that the decision\ndoes not conflict with any decision on the same question by the DM deciding the SS benefit.\n\n\n\nPeople admitted to hospital from care homes\n\n78710 In SPC there is no difference between the treatment of people in care homes and those living in\ntheir own homes (other than the deemed weekly income from capital limit). So when a person is admitted\nto hospital from a care home, the amount of any reduction in a claimant’s SPC will depend on\n\n\n1. the period for which the person receives, or is treated as receiving, free in-patient treatment (see DMG\n78795 and 78840 et seq) and\n\n\n2. whether the claimant has a partner who is a member of their household (see DMG 77128 et seq).\n\n\n78711 - 78719\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0115> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Free in-patient treatment 78720 - 78754 Deciding free in-patient treatment 78720 - 78721 Maintained free of charge 78722 - 78724 Medical or other treatment 78725 - 78730 Hospital or similar institution 78731 - 78737 Meaning of in-patient 78" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
