<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0143> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 13 Ch 78: State Pension Credit: additional amounts and special groups  — PDF page 143\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e10327f5069cdc54868955/dmg-Ch-78.pdf#page=143).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nRates from 8.4.19\n\nDeductions apply where\n\n\n\n1.   non-dependants aged 18 or over are in remunerative work - £100.65\n\n\n\n2.   the DM is satisfied that the non-dependant in remunerative work has a gross weekly income of\n\n\n2.1 Less than £143.00    £15.60\n\n\n2.2 £143.00 to £208.99 £35.85\n\n\n2.3 £209.00 to £271.99 £49.20\n\n\n2.4 £272.00 to £362.99 £80.55\n\n\n2.5 £363.00 to £450.99 £91.70\n\n\n2.6 £451.00 or more      £100.65\n\n\n\n\n3.   any other non-dependant aged 18 or over for whom deductions are relevant - £15.60.\n\n\n\n\nRates from 6.4.20\n\nDeductions apply where\n\n\n\n\n1.   non-dependants aged 18 or over are in remunerative work - £102.35\n\n\n\n\n2.   the DM is satisfied that the non-dependant in remunerative work has a gross weekly income of\n\n\n2.1 Less than £149.00 £15.85\n\n\n2.2 £149.00 to £216.99 £36.45\n\n\n2.3 £217.00 to £282.99 £50.05\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
