<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0145> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 13 Ch 78: State Pension Credit: additional amounts and special groups  — PDF page 145\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e10327f5069cdc54868955/dmg-Ch-78.pdf#page=145).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\n2.   the DM is satisfied that the non-dependant in remunerative work has a gross weekly income of\n\n\n2.1 Less than £154.00    £16.45\n\n\n2.2 £154.00 to £223.99 £37.80\n\n\n2.3 £224.00 to £291.99 £51.85\n\n\n2.4 £292.00 to £388.99 £84.85\n\n\n2.5 £389.00 to £483.99£96.60\n\n\n2.6 £484.00 or more      £106.05\n\n\n3.   any other non-dependant aged 18 or over for whom deductions are relevant - £16.45.\n\n\n\n\nRates from 10.4.23\n\n\n\nDeductions apply where\n\n\n\n\n1.   non-dependants aged 18 or over are in remunerative work - £116.75\n\n\n\n\n2.   the DM is satisfied that the non-dependant in remunerative work has a gross weekly income of\n\n\n2.1 Less than £162.00    £18.10\n\n\n2.2 £162.00 to £235.99 £41.60\n\n\n2.3 £236.00 to £307.99 £57.10\n\n\n2.4 £308.00 to £409.99 £93.40\n\n\n2.5 £410.00 to £510.99 £106.35\n\n\n2.6 £511.00 or more      £116.75\n\n\n3.   any other non-dependant aged 18 or over for whom deductions are relevant - £18.10.\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
