<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/83/0013> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 14 Ch 83: Assessed income periods — PDF page 13\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5aa9038ee5274a3e391e3e7c/dmgch83.pdf#page=13).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\n        Example\n\n        Henry aged 66 makes a claim for SPC on 10.3.09. He asks that his claim be\n        considered from 11.12.08.\n\n        The DM decides to backdate the claim by three months to 11.12.08.\n\n        On 17.3.09 the DM decides to award SPC to Henry and that it is payable from\n        15.12.08 (the first payday following 11.12.08).\n\n        The DM decides that he can set a five year AIP. He decides that the AIP starts on\n        11.12.08 and ends on 10.12.13.\n\n        Note: New claims to SPC with a TAM date on, or after 6.4.16 will have a 3 year PCR\n        set.\n\n        83048 - 83049\n\n\n\n\nVol 14 Amendment 40 June 2016\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
