<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/84/0040> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 14 Ch 84: Deemed weekly income from capital — PDF page 40\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a5e38bb8b7e4fa537e693d5/dmg-ch84.pdf#page=40).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nPayment made after Carer's Allowance reassessment following Sayce Review\n\n84365 A payment received on or after 16.7.26 following a recalculation of CA under the Sayce Review 1\n\nis disregarded indefinitely. Such a payment may be received where2\n\n\n1. a decision was made about the claimant’s CA entitlement due to fluctuating earnings between 10.4.15\nand 2.9.25 and\n\n\n2. that decision led to an overpayment of CA and\n\n\n3. following a reassessment conducted since 13.4.26 the Secretary of State determines that the\nclaimant’s earnings should have been averaged.\n\n\nNote: Arrears of CA that are not due to the reassessment exercise in 3. are not disregarded.\n\n\n                 1 Independent Review of Carer’s Allowance Overpayments; 2 SPC Regs, Sch V, para 20AB\n\n\nExample 1\n\n\nFreyja was in receipt of CA as a carer for her sister Greta but had also taken irregular shift work at a local\nconvenience store, so that her earnings fluctuated and occasionally exceeded the earnings limit for CA\nfour times in a nine-week period. On 10.12.24 a decision was made that Freyja had been overpaid\n£327.60 and that amount was recoverable as Freyja had not informed the Department of these earnings.\nHowever, after a review exercise concluded on 17.7.26 it was determined that, if the earnings had been\naveraged over the nine-week period, Freyja’s earnings would have been under the earnings limit. The\noverpayment is cancelled and Freyja is refunded £327.60, representing a restoration of her CA\nentitlement. The £327.60 is disregarded indefinitely from Freyja’s total capital when determining her\nSPC entitlement.\n\n\nExample 2\n\n\nAnton receives arrears of CA of £4,853.45 following a successful appeal to the FtT after his claim made\non 13.4.25 was refused. As these arrears are not associated with the Sayce Review they are included in\nfull in Anton’s capital from the date of receipt.\n\n\n84366 - 84370\n\n\n\n\nBusiness assets\n\nThe law\n84371 [See Memo DMG 13/20] The assets of a business are disregarded indefinitely if the person\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/84/0041> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "1. owns all or some of the assets and 2. works in the business as a S/E earner1. 1 SPC Regs, Sch V, Part I, para 9 84372 The assets are disregarded for a reasonable period to allow for them to be sold if the person 1. owns all or some of th" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
