<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/85/0089> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 14 Ch 85: Income other than earnings  — PDF page 89\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/690b7db588a98da87e292365/dmg-ch-85.pdf#page=89).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nDeprivation of income 85408 - 85439\n\n\n\nDeferral of retirement pension entitlement 85409 - 85410\n\n\nDeferral of State Pension entitlement 85411 - 85412\n\n\nDeprivation 85413\n\n\nMeaning of deprive 85414 - 85417\n\n\nQuestions for consideration 85418\n\n\nWas it the claimant’s income 85419 - 85420\n\n\nHas a deprivation of income happened 85421 - 85422\n\n\nWas the purpose of the deprivation to get or increase the amount of SPC 85423 - 85426\n\n\nTiming of the disposal 86427\n\n\nTrivial commutation of small pensions 86428 - 86429\n\n\nService users 86430 - 86439\n\n\n\n\n85408 DMs should treat claimants as receiving income that they have deprived themselves of for the\n\npurpose of gaining entitlement to or increasing the amount of SPC payable 1, unless the circumstances in\nDMG 85409 - 85410 or 85426 - 85434 apply.\n\n\n                                                                                     1 SPC Regs, reg 18(6)\n\n\n\nDeferral of retirement pension entitlement\n\n85409 From April 2005 pensioners can choose to be paid either an increased pension or a lump sum\npayment where they have deferred their entitlement to RP, shared additional pension or graduated\nretirement pension. Deferral has to be for at least twelve months (after 6.4.05) for the lump sum option\nto be available. Where someone dies whilst deferring, the surviving spouse or civil partner will have the\nsame choice in relation to the inherited increase or lump sum.\n\n\n\n\n85410 The rule regarding deprivation of income at DMG 85408 shall not apply1 if a claimant\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
