<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/86/0013> <https://schema.org/pagination> "13"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/86/0013> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 14 Ch 86: Earnings  — PDF page 13\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/698462dd468d351e1406b4a7/dmgch86.pdf#page=13).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nIntroduction 86028 - 86030\n\n\n\n86028 This part deals with the calculation and treatment of payments made to SPC claimants who are\nemployed earners. These will usually be earnings paid by an employer, but may be other types of\npayment.\n\n\n86029 How payments made to employees affect a claim to SPC will depend on\n\n\n1. whether the work is continuing or\n\n\n2. whether the work has ended.\n\n\n86030 Earnings from employment as an employed earner which is ongoing whilst the claimant is in\nreceipt of SPC are taken into account, less any appropriate earnings disregard, in the same way as other\nincome.\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/86/0014> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Earnings of employed earners - explanation of terms 86031 - 86037 Meaning of employed earner 86031 - 86033 Meaning of earnings 86034 - 86035 Meaning of derived from 86036 Meaning of Gross earnings 86037 Meaning of employed earner 86031 The " <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
