<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/86/0040> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 14 Ch 86: Earnings  — PDF page 40\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/698462dd468d351e1406b4a7/dmgch86.pdf#page=40).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nPayments on termination of employment 86150 - 86199\n\n\n\nGeneral 86150 - 86152\n\n\nPayments in lieu of remuneration 86153 - 86155\n\n\nPayments in lieu of notice 86156 - 86159\n\n\nHoliday pay 86160 - 86161\n\n\nStatutory redundancy payments 86162 - 86169\n\n\n\n\nGeneral\n\n86150 Any earnings derived from employment which ended before the day that the claimant first\n\nsatisfies the conditions of entitlement to an award of SPC should be disregarded in full 1. But this\ndisregard does not apply to the payments described at DMG 86062.The disregard can apply to\nsuccessive awards of SPC.\n\n\n                                                                                  1 SPC Regs, Sch VI, para 6\n\n\nExample\n\n\nCharles’ employment ends on 1.6.15. He claims and is entitled to an award of SPC from 2.6.15. The DM\ncan apply the disregard in DMG 86150 to earnings derived from that employment. At a later stage\nCharles’ award of SPC comes to an end because he starts a new job and his earnings exceed the AMG.\nAfter a few months, this second employment also comes to an end and Charles reclaims SPC for a\nsecond time. The DM can apply the disregard in DMG 86150 to earnings derived from this second\nemployment which has now just ended.\n\n\n86151 Employees may be entitled to certain payments when their employment ends. These include\n\n\n1. PILOR (see DMG 86153)\n\n\n2. PILON (see DMG 86156)\n\n\n3. holiday pay (see DMG 86070 and 86160)\n\n\n4. statutory redundancy payments (see DMG 86162).\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/86/0041> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "86152 How such payments affect a claim for SPC depends on 1. what type of payment is involved 2. when the payment is due to be made 3. when the work ended. Payments in lieu of remuneration 86153 PILOR is paid in place of a person's normal w" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/86/0041> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "page/86/0041" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/86/0041> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/chapter/86> <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/86/0041> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/> <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
