<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/86/0064> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 14 Ch 86: Earnings  — PDF page 64\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/698462dd468d351e1406b4a7/dmgch86.pdf#page=64).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nCalculation of income tax, Social Security contributions and qualifying\npremium 86470 - 86529\n\n\n\nIntroduction 86470 - 86479\n\n\nChargeable income 86480 - 86489\n\n\nDeduction for notional income tax 86490 - 86499\n\n\nDeduction for notional Class 2 Social Security contributions 86500 - 86509\n\n\nDeduction for notional Class 4 Social Security contributions 86510 - 86519\n\n\nPremiums for personal pension schemes and retirement annuity contracts 86520 - 86529\n\n\n\n\nIntroduction\n\n86470 Having calculated the gross receipts and expenses from self-employment on a cash flow basis,\n\nthe DM should consider deductions for 1\n\n\n1. income tax (see DMG 86490 et seq) and\n\n\n2. Class 2 SS contributions (see DMG 86500 at seq) and\n\n\n3. Class 4 SS contributions (see DMG 86510 et seq) and\n\n\n4. half of any premium for a\n\n\n      4.1 personal pension scheme (see DMG 86521) or\n\n\n      4.2 retirement annuity contract (see DMG 86523).\n\n\n                                                                1 SS Ben (C of E) Regs, reg 13(4)(b) & (c)\n\n\n86471 The DM should base deductions for DMG 86470 1. - 3. on the chargeable income for the\nassessment period.\n\n\n86472 - 86479\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
