<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/86/0072> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 14 Ch 86: Earnings  — PDF page 72\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/698462dd468d351e1406b4a7/dmgch86.pdf#page=72).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\nParticular forms of self-employment 86530 - 86699\n\n\n\nChild minders 86530 - 86539\n\n\nCrofts or small holdings 86540 - 86544\n\n\nFarmers 86545 - 86549\n\n\nHotels, guest houses, bed and breakfast establishments 86550 - 86555\n\n\nLocal exchange trading systems 86556 - 86569\n\n\nPartnerships 86570 - 86589\n\n\nRenting out property as a business 86590 - 86599\n\n\nSeasonally self-employed 86600 - 86604\n\n\nSub Contractors 86605 - 86606\n\n\nActors and entertainers 86607 - 86618\n\n\nShare Fishermen 86619 - 86699\n\n\n\n\nChild minders\n\n86530 A child minder is a person who engages in a contract for services to care for another person's\nchild in return for payment. Most child minders\n\n\n1. work from their own homes and\n\n\n2. are registered with the LA and\n\n\n3. are restricted to the number of children they care for at any one time.\n\n\n86531 To calculate a child minder's normal weekly earnings the DM should\n\n\n1. determine the assessment period in the normal way and\n\n\n2. calculate the gross receipts for that period and\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
