<https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/86/0089> <https://schema.org/text> "# DMG Vol 14 Ch 86: Earnings  — PDF page 89\n\n[Verify the official PDF page](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/698462dd468d351e1406b4a7/dmgch86.pdf#page=89).\n\n> Extracted source text. Layout and reading order may differ from the PDF. This project does not establish current entitlement or law.\n\n```text\n2. Income tax is payable on taxable income\n\n\nNote: There are different rates for Scotland from 18/19 – see 3. below.\n\n\n\n\n                £\n\n\n                1 - £37,400            at basic rate of 20%\n\n\n10/11           over £37,400           higher rate of 40%\n\n\n                over £150,000          additional rate of 50%\n\n\n                1 - £35,000            at basic rate of 20%\n\n\n11/12           over £35,000           higher rate of 40%\n\n\n                over £150,000          additional rate of 50%\n\n\n                1 - £34,370            at basic rate of 20%\n\n\n12/13           over £34,370           higher rate of 40%\n\n\n                over £150,000          additional rate of 50%\n\n\n                1 - £32,010            at basic rate of 20%\n\n\n13/14           over £32,010           higher rate of 40%\n\n\n                over £150,000          additional rate of 45%\n\n\n                1 - £31,865            at basic rate of 20%\n14/15\n                over £31,865           higher rate of 40%\n\n\n                1 - £31,785            at basic rate of 20%\n15/16\n                over £31,785           higher rate of 40%\n\n\n                1 - £32,000            at basic rate of 20%\n16/17\n                over £32,000           higher rate of 40%\n\n```\n" <https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/bundle/pension-credit> .
